<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1181/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1181/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1181/>;
    dc:modified '2019-11-25T15:28:56'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'epitoke'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A life stage of aquatic polychaete worms whose life cycle include a process known as "epitoky". Epitoky is the metamorphosis of a sexually immature worm (the atoke) into a sexually mature form (the epitoke) adapted for a brief free-swimming near-surface phase.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1181'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1180/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1180/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1180/>;
    dc:modified '2019-11-15T17:58:54'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'pupa'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An organism at the pupal stage. A life stage of some insects undergoing a complete metamorphosis between immature (larva) and mature (adult or imago) stages.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1180'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1179/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1179/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1179/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-29T18:04:40'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ephyrula'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ephyra'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A free-swimming precursor stage of the adult medusa stage, ephyrae (or ephyrulae) are small medusae ("medusoid heads") that separate from the polyp by budding in a process known as strobilation before metamorphosing into scyphomedusae, the life stage of the adult medusa typically identified as jellyfish. Strobils can sometimes become scyphomedusae without passing through the ephyra stage.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1179'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1178/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1178/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1178/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-23T13:28:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'cercaria'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A free-swimming larval stage of trematodes (also known as parasitic flatworms or flukes) during which the parasitic fluke typically passes from an intermediate host (often a snail) to another intermediate host or to the final vertebrate host. Cercaria can develop from the sporocyst stage or from the redial stage of the trematode depending on species.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1178'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1177/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1177/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1177/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-23T13:20:27'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sporocyst'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A term used for a development stage in the lifecycle of Apicomplexa parasites and trematode flatworm parasites (flukes). In the trematodes lifecycle it is an elongated sac-like structure that is formed in the initial stage of infection of an intermediate host (typically a snail). It develops from a miracidium and evolve into a redia.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1177'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1176/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1176/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1176/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-23T13:10:12'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'metacercaria'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A resting late larval stage of the digenetic trematodes (digeneans) with a three-host life cycle. It is a tailless stage which develops in the intermediate host either encysted in a cyst or encapsulated in a layer of host tissue. This is usually the form which is infective to the definitive host when it ingests the infected intermediate host.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1176'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1175/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1175/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1175/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-23T13:04:46'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'cercaria purpurea'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The larval stage of the trematode Parorchis acanthus (urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:158687), a parasitic castrator of the common periwinkle Littorina littorea (urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:140262). Trematoda is a clade within the phylum Platyhelminthes. It includes two groups of parasitic flatworms, known as flukes. They are internal parasites of molluscs and vertebrates.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1175'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1174/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1174/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1174/>;
    dc:modified '2019-08-23T12:59:58'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'scyphistoma'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The fixed segmented polyp-like stage in the life cycle of a jellyfish, which reproduces asexually by budding (strobilation).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1174'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1173/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1173/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/S11/current/S1173/>;
    dc:modified '2019-07-16T18:46:08'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'smolt'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A young salmon or sea-going trout that is at the stage of development when it assumes a silvery color and is physiologically ready to migrate to the sea.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S11::S1173'^^xsd:string .
